PR checklist:

- [x] Purpose of the code is [evident to future readers](https://semgrep.dev/docs/contributing/contributing-code/#explaining-code)
- [x] Tests included or PR comment includes a reproducible test plan
- [x] Documentation is up-to-date
- [x] A changelog entry was [added to changelog.d](https://semgrep.dev/docs/contributing/contributing-code/#adding-a-changelog-entry) for any user-facing change
- [x] Change has no security implications (otherwise, ping security team)

If you're unsure on any of this, please see:

- [Contribution guidelines](https://semgrep.dev/docs/contributing/contributing-code)!
- [One of the more specific guides located here](https://semgrep.dev/docs/contributing/contributing/)

This PR introduces a new feature in MMH that allows authorised users to add new assets.

- Some fields in the form are required and always present, while there are fields (such as estate, block, no of bedrooms, living rooms etc) that may or may not show up depending on the Asset Type selected;
- This conditional behaviour is controlled mainly by the contents of the `asset-type.ts` file;
- If applicable, it will be possible to 'link' the new asset to an Estate, a Block and a Sub-block;
- The managing organisation field is a 'select' type of field, and based on the choice, of this, a `managingOrganisationId` is selected. These are hardcoded in a file called `managing-organisations.ts`;
- Errors implemented for required fields, if a value is not provided;
- The postcode input is checked using a regex, and numerical fields only allow positive numbers;
- The feature is only available for authorised users in specific Google groups. These Google groups are defined in AWS Parameter Store:
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/70756861/231518040-bc291d5a-889b-440c-9c53-2738e583e478.png)
- An error message is shown in case the API request to create the new asset fails:
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/70756861/231518822-2d19c140-946a-4d71-94be-9e4822b13f20.png)
- A success message is shown when the API request to create the new asset succeeds;
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/70756861/231731609-9de1f0e7-1d7f-4b89-9e03-8afff0c37087.png)
- Added some unit tests for this however most of the tests will be added as E2E tests in the dedicated repo.

